Reason: emit one parquet row per scored query into the shared ranks/ schema; dump only, the ranking itself is untouched. TRIX's compute_ranking and strict_negative_mask are byte-identical to ULTRA's and its test() differs from ULTRA's only by deleted comments, so the rank definition carries over unchanged. The dump directory arrives by environment variable rather than by flag: run_entity.py builds its parser from the config's template variables and marks every one required, so a new flag would have to be threaded through the config to be accepted at all.

